The rule for k_recovery says the object recovered is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text. For the original text fence[ A ] S, the fence holds object A, so k_recovery returns A. For the rewritten text fence[ A ] S B, the fence still holds only A, and B is after the fence, so the last object inside a code fence is still A. Therefore k_recovery is unchanged between the two texts.